  "problem": "C62 only let contending workers help; idle workers could not drain remaining exact prerequisites during a long outer anchor.",
  "implementation": "A per-root Rayon scope exposes bounded drain tasks on the existing pool. A typed Evaluation borrows the planner and scope; spawned closures construct their own Evaluation. Permits cap queued/running drains at the current pool size, retire under the enqueue mutex, and release on panic/error. Drains return when no eligible work exists. A thread-local stack of live queue identities and owned dependency levels prevents a drain inherited at a nested join from executing its suspended same-job ancestor. Required cell waits keep strictly earlier helping. Temporary writer look-ahead is bounded to 32 positions, with full source-ordered consumption across batches.",
