    "scope_lifetimes": "Planner lives outside a per-root rayon::scope. Short-lived Evaluation borrows the planner and Scope. Spawn closures capture the planner and create their own Evaluation from the Scope argument. No unsafe scope or context lifetime casts.",
    "permits": "At most current pool thread count of queued/running drains. Offer/reserve and last-helper empty exit synchronize with the same mutex. RAII releases permit on errors/panic. No sleeping drain loop.",
    "ancestor_protection": "Per-thread stack records queue identity and owned cell level. A scoped drain inherited at a nested join may pop only anchors strictly earlier than its suspended same-job initializer. Other jobs have separate identities. Cooperative cell waits retain stricter waiting-cell levels. Guard pop executes in release builds too.",
    "ownership": "Every spawned helper joins in the root scope before publication and before error cleanup. Queue stores only keys. Results/errors remain single-initializer cached values.",
    "temporary_memory": "Expose batches of at most 32 writer positions; fully consume every original writer in order across batches. Queue still capped at 4096 keys, original direct resolution on saturation. ColumnCell remains 32 bytes, versus 24 in accepted C60. TLS retains only small scalar key/level stacks.",
    "instrumentation": "cfg(test) target/helper task counts are separate. Helper events include prerequisite root. Physical-thread interval unions include both kinds. Completion percentiles and longest targets exclude helpers; final tail runs to last target or helper finish.",
    "call_path_audit": "Discovery::plans uses plans_inner(... parallel=false ...) and portals::prepare loops serially. Anchor replay and terrain-job bodies contain no explicit Rayon yielding, but dynamic guard also protects a scoped drain inherited at a future/nested join.",
    "required_followup": [
      "Complete test and GPU parity results",
      "Full original and C60 decompressed NBT",
      "Paired ordinary and task-phase attribution",
      "Real reverse and 2/4/8 simultaneous region requests if selected",
      "Sustained memory and real lifecycle if selected",
      "Quiet final confirmation remains deferred"
    ],
    "fixture_compile_fix": "126b379 tests-first.log: idle-worker test borrowed an mpsc Receiver across a Send Rayon closure. d5b6d07 moves receiver ownership into the scope and borrows the externally owned cells. No production code change.",
    "rayon_source_audit": "Installed rayon-core 1.13.0 scope/mod.rs lines 523-538: spawn creates a HeapJob and injects/pushes it; it does not synchronously invoke the task body. Scope provides the join/lifetime guarantee.",
    "reviewed_risks": [
      "Global queue and extra scoped-task scheduling may cost more than exposed parallelism.",
      "TLS push/pop is on new cell initialization, not on ready scalar reads; its cost must be included in ordinary timings.",
      "The inherited-initializer guard constrains a drain on the current physical thread for this job; other job identities do not suppress their work.",
      "Failure may leave queued descriptors/uninitialized slots, but scope joins running work and the existing failed Planner drop owns all cleanup.",
      "Helper counters count descriptor processing, including already-complete/in-flight keys; they do not measure fresh construction or CPU utilization."
    ]
