  "observer_definition": "Target/helper counts and longest tasks are separate. Physical-thread unions include both; target completion percentiles exclude helpers, while the tail ends at the last target/helper completion. In-flight spans include blocking/preemption and are not CPU utilization. Process CPU includes service/GPU/observer threads. Separate C60/C62/C63 observer runs are not causal speedup comparisons.",
  "decision": "Hold unmerged. The second standard seed and custom-bounds case lose throughput in the paired observations, and main has a worse p95 despite a lower median. Known host load precludes quiet acceptance; these results do not establish a consistent benefit that selects this scheduler or its extra cell memory.",
  "next_experiment": "Try nonblocking claims for optional scoped helpers: ready values return immediately, an empty cell may be claimed, and an already-owned key is skipped without waiting. Required consumers continue to wait/help and still resolve every exact writer. Count actual scoped ready/busy/owned outcomes at the claim site before attributing helper counts to useful work. Preserve cached errors, panic recovery, source ordering and scoped joins. See external helper-ownership-hypothesis.md.",
  "limitations": [
    "Known unrelated host load; quiet final confirmation remains deferred by user.",
    "Descriptor counters include ready/in-flight work and do not establish fresh initialization or useful parallel CPU time.",
    "Optional drains currently use the blocking anchor path. Shared contended-cell notifications wake all job waiters; possible extra wake/recheck cost remains an unquantified hypothesis.",
    "No reverse/concurrent/portal/retention acceptance was run for this unselected prototype.",
    "The full subsecond median/p95, no-regression, concurrency and sustained-memory goal remains open."
  ],
